# What `gcloud builds submit .` must not upload.
#
# Cloud Build tars this directory into a GCS staging bucket and keeps it in build
# history. Anything here that is a credential stays readable there after the build,
# so this file is the durable version of "remember to delete the key first".
#
# Note: creating this file makes gcloud stop consulting .gitignore on its own, so the
# include below is what keeps those rules in force. Do not remove it.
#!include:.gitignore

# Never upload the repository history. Nothing in infra/cloudbuild.yaml reads .git,
# and it is usually the largest single directory here.
.git/
.gitignore

# Credentials. Deliberately broader than what is in the tree today: a key that has not
# been created yet is the one this is for. A service account key sat in this repo root
# and would have been uploaded before this file existed.
*-sa-key*.json
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
*accessKeys*.csv
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Operator artifacts. Large, local, and meaningless to a build.
backups/
skills-pvc-backup-*/
skills-pvc-backup-*.tar.gz
skills-backuo-*.tar.gz
*.tar.gz
trace-*.json
outputs/
.playwright-mcp/
claude-design/

# Root-level screenshots and scratch notes. Scoped to the root with a leading slash so
# images the frontend actually ships are still uploaded.
/*.png
/result.md

# Agent and tooling state.
.claude/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/

# Kept by the include above, restated because losing either one is expensive:
#   env/**/*.env          - local secrets
#   skills/.governed-versions/ - runtime blob store; the deploy must never push it,
#                                and sync-skills-pvc must never delete it
